IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei6-schedule-rows`
IMPORT `ei6-schedule-i`

-- Tests of Schedule I (src:3201-3245). Every expected value is read off the printed table by hand: the row is the
-- hours of insurable employment, the column is the band of the regional rate of unemployment, counted from the left
-- (1 = "6% and under", 2 = "More than 6% but not more than 7%", ... 12 = "More than 16%").
-- A rate is a fraction: 13.5% is 0.135.

§ `Schedule I - the rows and their edges`

-- Row 420-454 (src:3205): eight blank cells, then 26, 28, 30, 32 in columns 9 to 12.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 420 (13.5%) EQUALS JUST 26
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 420 (14.5%) EQUALS JUST 28
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 420 (15.5%) EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 420 (20%) EQUALS JUST 32
-- A blank cell: column 8 (more than 12% but not more than 13%) of row 420-454.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 420 (12.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The rate 13% exactly belongs to column 8 ("not more than 13%"), which is blank in this row; 13.01% is column 9.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 420 (13%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 420 (13.01%) EQUALS JUST 26
-- Fewer than 420 hours: no row (fork F-ei6-8): NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 419 (20%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 0 (20%) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The edge between row 420-454 and row 455-489 (src:3206: 24 in column 8, so 12.5% gives a number only from 455).
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 454 (12.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 455 (12.5%) EQUALS JUST 24
-- A count of hours between the two rows (454.5) belongs to the lower row: fork F-ei6-8.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 454.5 (12.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 489 (12.5%) EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 490 (12.5%) EQUALS JUST 25

§ `Schedule I - the first row that has a number in every column, and the rate edges`

-- Row 630-664 (src:3211): two blank cells, then 17 in column 3.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 630 (6.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 630 (7.5%) EQUALS JUST 17
-- Row 665-699 (src:3212): one blank cell, then 15 in column 2.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 665 (5%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 699 (6.5%) EQUALS JUST 15
-- Row 700-734 (src:3213): 14, 16, 18, ... 36 in columns 1 to 12.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 700 (5%) EQUALS JUST 14
-- 6% exactly is "6% and under" (column 1); more than 6% is column 2.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 700 (6%) EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 700 (6.01%) EQUALS JUST 16
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 700 (7%) EQUALS JUST 16
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 700 (9.5%) EQUALS JUST 22
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 734 (16%) EQUALS JUST 34
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 734 (16.01%) EQUALS JUST 36
-- Row 735-769 (src:3214) repeats row 700-734.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 735 (5%) EQUALS JUST 14
-- Row 770-804 (src:3215): 15, 17, ... 37.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 770 (5%) EQUALS JUST 15
-- Row 1015-1049 (src:3222): 18, 20, 22, 24, ... 40.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1015 (5%) EQUALS JUST 18
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1049 (8.5%) EQUALS JUST 24

§ `Schedule I - the rows where the number stops growing at 45`

-- Row 1400-1434 (src:3233): 24, 26, ... 44, 45.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1434 (5%) EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1434 (15.5%) EQUALS JUST 44
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1434 (16.5%) EQUALS JUST 45
-- Row 1435-1469 (src:3234): 25, 27, ... 43, 45, 45.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1435 (5%) EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1435 (15.5%) EQUALS JUST 45
-- Row 1785-1819 (src:3244): 35, 37, 39, 41, 43, 45, 45, ...
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1785 (5%) EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1819 (10.5%) EQUALS JUST 45
-- A count between rows 1785-1819 and 1820- (1819.5) belongs to the lower row: fork F-ei6-8.
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1819.5 (5%) EQUALS JUST 35
-- Last row, 1820 and more (src:3245): 36, 38, 40, 42, 44, 45, ...
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1820 (5%) EQUALS JUST 36
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1820 (9.5%) EQUALS JUST 44
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 1820 (10.5%) EQUALS JUST 45
#ASSERT `Act Schedule I the maximum number of weeks of benefits` 5000 (5%) EQUALS JUST 36
